From efc78d4384e14f6711f065eb7f904f8a27ef5e15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuriy Kapoyko <yury.kapoyko@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:09:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ggml cuda: isolate optional padded GQA-6 tile fold

Place the six real query heads of the supported GQA-6/head-256/native-Q8_0
geometry in one padded eight-column tile block (ncols1 1, ncols2 8), reducing
three logical KV traversals per query row to one. Padded columns receive zero
Q and are never stored; padding-only warps still join cooperative K/V loads
and barriers but skip KQ/softmax/VKQ arithmetic.

The fold lives in a dedicated self-contained kernel TU
(fattn-tile-gqa6-fold.cuh + one generated instance). Ordinary tile
instantiations carry no fold template parameter and compile to baseline
device code byte-identically; shared changes are host-only (force_split
plumbing compiled out via if constexpr, dispatch + census). This removes the
ordinary-kernel codegen perturbation that exposed intermittent gfx1102
BF16/D=96 corruption, and the template-parameter conflict with optional 0101.

Optional and default OFF: GGML_HIP_FA_TILE_GQA6_FOLD=1 opts in (read once per
process), gated to GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_RDNA3_0. A one-shot INFO census at -lv 4
proves the folded arm launched. Adds head-256/GQA-6 coverage: inert boundary
widths 9..16, deep KV 32768, and the derived-mask form.

Assisted-by: Qwen4-Max
